description:
src/cache.rs:182-188: the trait docstring says:

    /// get_crl / get_ocsp MUST return None for entries whose next_update is
    /// in the past.

But 'in the past' relative to WHAT? The reference impl uses SystemTime::now() — wall-clock — while the wrapper carries a caller-supplied now_unix. A custom RevocationCache impl reading this docstring has no way to know which clock the trait contract refers to.

This is the rustdoc half of PKIX-f1j4.1 (the correctness issue). Fixing the correctness bug (thread now_unix through the cache) will fix the docstring too. Filing separately so the reviewer doesn't accept a 'documented as wall-clock, behaviour stays as wall-clock' resolution to the correctness bug.

Whatever the trait contract decides, name the time source explicitly: 'in the past relative to <X>' where X is either the caller-supplied validation time or a documented wall-clock fallback.
